version 0.19.0
module charger-power

# The BQ24610 charge and power path (datasheet SLUS892D Figure 20): 19V adapter, 3-cell Li-ion
# (12.6V), 2A adapter limit, 1.9A charge, 0.19A precharge/termination, 5.2-hour safety timer.
#
# Those numbers are what the circuit sets, read off SLUS892D: Eq. 2 gives the charge current,
# Eq. 4 the precharge and termination current, Eq. 6 the safety timer. With the sense resistor
# the design uses (RSR = R22 = 10mOhm) and VREF = 2.1V: VISET1 = 2.1V x 22.1k / (100k + 22.1k) =
# 0.380V, so ICHARGE = 0.380V / (20 x 10mOhm) = 1.9A; VISET2 = 2.1V x 10k / (100k + 10k) =
# 0.191V, so IPRECHARGE = ITERM = 0.191V / (100 x 10mOhm) = 0.19A; CTTC = 56nF and KTTC =
# 5.6min/nF give 5.2 hours.
#
# The adapter's limit is 2A, so the charger's own input current limit is set below it: IDPM =
# VACSET / (20 x RAC) = 0.395V / (20 x 10mOhm) = 1.98A, with R3 = 100k from VREF and R4 = 23.2k
# to ground. A 1.9A charge current into a 12.6V pack draws 1.37A at 19V, so the adapter is not
# the binding constraint and the input current regulation never has to give up charge current.
#
# The adapter's return is the board's ground: the jack's sleeve (J1.2) is on GND. SLUS892D feeds
# VCC through R17 from the input FETs' common-source node (AC_COMMON), and that node sits at the
# adapter's *positive* rail — the sleeve does not belong there.
#
# The adapter's positive rail is a declared window, not a comment: 0V..19V (see the constraints
# below). The input FETs' gate node rides between the two rails it is wired to -- ground through
# the charger's ACDRV, AC_COMMON through R14 -- so it carries the same window.
#
# The module owns its refdes and net names; the board reaches it through its ports
# (spec/module.md §3). Its nets are flattened to M1.<net> unless a port merges them into a
# board-level net.
instances
  C1    IDm78w8s  cap-mlcc-0402       100n    10%    25V  X7R
  C2    ID6ges83  cap-mlcc-0402       100n    10%    50V  X7R
  C3    IDyvrjy7  cap-mlcc-0402       100n    10%    50V  X7R
